  "notes": [
    "One scripted local trial, not model decision quality or statistical evidence. Parent full-suite work overlapped this period; timings are indicative.",
    "All three arms use the same exact typed source rows. Projection, imports, and the rolling-source update are common acquisition/rebinding work outside measured MCP plan-reuse calls.",
    "Discovery is measured over one saved skill. This does not establish discovery ranking quality over a large skill library.",
    "The transfer comparison reuses a plan with different explicit immutable bindings. A stable recurring task with a rolling logical source is cheaper and is reported separately.",
    "Random immutable IDs affect tokenization; projected amortization uses this single observed per-transfer difference, not a guarantee for other workflows.",
    "An initial pilot failed the retained receipt check because a one-row projection lacked ORDER BY. The final plan explicitly orders it, and a focused regression verifies reuse. The failure and corrected pilot traces remain local.",
    "Public evidence includes aggregate results and checks only, not individual taxi trip rows, local absolute paths, generated workspace identifiers, or credentials."
  ]
